'' VIRTUAL and ABSTRACT come last in the modifier run, belong to a member of a type, and
'' are not for a constructor. 'const virtual' leads with const and is accepted; 'virtual
'' const', 'virtual static', 'static virtual' and 'virtual abstract' are fbc error 17, a
'' loose one at module level is 17, an abstract/virtual constructor is 210/211 and an
'' abstract destructor is 212 -- while a VIRTUAL destructor is the ordinary case.
''
'' NOT MODELLED: fbc's error 219 for VIRTUAL on a definition whose declaration was not
'' virtual. That is a question about the declaration, not about this syntax, and reading
'' it as one refused two of this suite's own tests that fbc compiles.
'' Matches fbc line for line -- 18, 19, 20, 21, 22, 23, 26.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/diagnostics/src/virtual-placement.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' GOLDEN: expected/virtual-placement.out
